sections.wikitext:
The song reached number one on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] chart and number two on the [[UK singles chart]] for two weeks in late October and early November 1987.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.officialcharts.com/charts/singles-chart/19871101/7501/|title=Official Singles Chart|website=Official Charts Company|date=31 October 1987|access-date=8 April 2020}}</ref>

On the ''Billboard'' Hot 100 chart, "Faith" went from number 54 to number 37, the week of 31 October 1987. It reached number one on 12 December 1987 and remained there for four consecutive weeks. Altogether, "Faith" stayed in the top 10 for nine weeks, the top 20 for 11 weeks and the top 40 for 15 weeks.{{citation needed|date=April 2020}}

In [[Canada]], it spent 12 weeks at number one, the longest run at the top in the 1980's, according to ''[[The Record (magazine)|The Record]]''<ref>{{cite book|author=Nanda Lwin|author-link=Nanda Lwin|title=Top 40 Hits: The Essential Chart Guide|publisher=Music Data Canada|year=1999|isbn=1-896594-13-1}}</ref>.

